<title>FRANCE: France to sell 20 to 22 bln Ffr of bonds Thursday.</title>
<headline>France to sell 20 to 22 bln Ffr of bonds Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France is to offer between 20 and 22 billion francs of government bonds at its next scheduled auction on Thursday, of which four to six billion francs will be in the variable-rate TEC 10, the Treasury said on Monday.</p>
<p>On offer will be the new 10-year benchmark, the 5.50 percent April 25, 2007 OAT, and the TEC 10.</p>
<p>Payment date for both lines is January 27.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
